{{DISPLAYTITLE: <span style="color: #b300b3;">Rage</span>}}
{{Protection}}{{MagicWords}}{{ClashofClansLink|Rage Spell}}

{{Card Infobox|Cost=2|Rarity=Epic|Type=Spell|Arena=Serenity Peak|ReleaseDate=4 January 2016}}
{{Quote|Increases troop movement and attack speed. Buildings attack faster and summon troops quicker, too. Chaaaarge!}}

The Rage is an {{Rarity|Epic}} [[Cards|card]] that is unlocked from the [[Arenas|Serenity Peak (Arena 14)]]. It is an area-damage, air-targeting [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] with a medium radius and low damage. It increases the movement speed and attack speed of allied [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] and [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]] by 30%. It is a deep purple potion packed in a large bottle. It is also the same as that spawned by the [[Lumberjack]] and the [[Santa Hog Rider]]. A Rage card costs 2 [[Elixir]] to deploy.

==Modifiers==
===[[File:Rage Common Modifier.png|45x45px]] Common: Raging Rage===
{{Quote|+200% radius}}
Rage's area radius is increased by 200%, for a total of 9 tiles. Its damage is also increased.

===[[File:Rage Rare Modifier.png|45x45px]] Rare: Just Superhero Stuff===
{{Quote|Super Rage buff}}
The Rage's boost is increased.

===[[File:Rage Epic Modifier.png|45x45px]] Epic: Keep Calm & Rage On===
{{Quote|Infinite Rage buff}}
Rage's duration after leaving the radius is increased to infinite seconds.

==Strategy==
{{Battle Deck with Card|:Category:Battle Decks using the Rage Card}}
*The Rage can be used to increase the movement speed of slow [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]], such as [[Golem]]s, [[P.E.K.K.A.|P.E.K.K.A]]s, [[Giant]]s, [[Giant Skeleton]]s, [[Electro Giant]]s, [[Elixir Golem]]s, [[Valkyrie]]s, [[Mighty Miner]]s, and [[Lava Hound]]s.
*This [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] can also be used to boost the spawn speeds of [[cards]] such as the [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Witch]], and [[Night Witch]], the fire rate of defensive [[:Category:Building Cards|buildings]], or the [[Elixir Collector]]'s production speed. However, building lifetime still drops with its normal rate, even with the Rage, so beware when using it on low-health buildings. It should also never be used on the [[Goblin Cage]], as the Goblin Brawler only spawns after it is destroyed. 
**When used with Barbarian Hut, it will result in the last wave spawning 3 [[Barbarians]] instead of 1. The death spawn Barbarian will also spawn afterwards for extra defense. This is a 2 Elixir investment for an equivalent return value of 2 Elixir, and thus it can be worth using if the player wants to make use of the last wave of Barbarians in defense.
*Rage can be used to help fast attacks, and with its low cost, it can assist the [[Mini P.E.K.K.A.|Mini P.E.K.K.A]], [[Prince]], [[Hog Rider]], [[Ram Rider]], [[Elite Barbarians]], and other troops to destroy a [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Tower]]. It is particularly effective when the opponent's best counter to the attack is out of hand, forcing them to quickly react with a different card.
*In addition to their normal attack speed, the Rage can also increase the speed of the first attack for troops, allowing them to retarget to other troops faster. For example, against a [[Skeleton Army]], ranged troops like the [[Musketeer]], [[Dart Goblin]], [[Archers]], [[Cannon Cart]], and [[Electro Wizard]] will be able to defeat more [[Skeletons]] compared to a non-raged one.
*Rage does a small amount of damage when used, which is enough to defeat anything up to [[Spear Goblins]]. This is enough to allow troops to break through weak swarms while also getting their speed and attack speed boosted.
**The [[Goblin Curse]] synergizes well with Rage, as Rage instantly turns any troops defeated within the radius of the curse into [[Goblins]], which are immediately boosted by the Rage and can quickly overwhelm the enemy's Crown Tower if they don't have a spell prepared.
*Rage works well in [[Goblin Giant]] [[Battle Decks|decks]], as the Goblin Giant is faster than other tanks, allowing him to reach the Crown Tower much sooner and deal significantly more damage. The Goblin Giant also comes with 3 different attackers that benefit from the spell, making him a better choice than other troops. A Ram Rider and [[Goblin Machine]] can benefit in a similar way.
*The effect of Rage falls off after 1 second after something has left its radius, and will always expire once the spell's duration ends. This matters the most on short-ranged cards like [[Balloon]] as they would not be able to take full advantage of the spell, restricting the spell's placement as a result.
*When used on cards with a ramp-up mechanic like the [[Inferno Tower]], [[Inferno Dragon]], and [[Mighty Miner]], the Rage will allow them to reach their next tier faster. This can be key in situations where there is something that is following the tank, allowing the Inferno Tower to defeat its support troops as well instead of just the tank.
*Rage does not affect animations occurring after set periods, nor can it influence anything irrelevant to movement or direct attacks. For example, the [[Executioner]]'s axe flies at the same speed even if the Executioner is raged, the [[King's Tower]] will not activate its cannon more quickly, and the [[Giant Skeleton]]'s or Balloon's death bomb will not explode faster, so raging these units would be less effective. 
**The only exception is the [[Phoenix]]'s Egg; Rage allows it to revive faster. However, it will still be destroyed solo by the [[Tower Princess]] if nothing is tanking for the Egg.
*It is effective when the player is defending their Crown Towers since it will be able to affect both the defensive units and buildings.
*Rage can be quite effective in [[Goblin Barrel]] decks, as its unrestricted deployment allows it to be placed directly on the Goblin Barrel when attacking the Crown Tower, boosting the attack speed of the Goblins while also defeating or weakening enemy swarms like the [[Goblin Gang]]. Unlike the [[Giant Snowball]], it does not have to travel to reach the target, and unlike the [[Zap]], it does not force the Crown Tower to retarget on the Goblins when used in conjunction with a tank. However, these combos should only be done if opposing spells are not in rotation.
*Inherently, the Rage is a high-risk, high-reward card that requires good timing in order to succeed. When using Rage, be careful to time it right or else an opposing counterattack will come unhindered due to the player's lack of [[Elixir]].
*Rage can be used for the player’s troops to dodge slow-moving spells, especially ones with a small radius, like the [[Rocket]]. This is effective with the [[Three Musketeers]], [[Baby Dragon]], and Balloon.
**However, the Rage's 0.5 second deploy time gives more time for the spell to reach said troop. Timing the Rage is very important, especially with slower moving troops.
**Similarly, it can allow troops to escape a [[Poison]] and Goblin Curse, as well as neutralize the slow effect of the former. However, it is a heavy Elixir investment.
*The [[Lumberjack]] is an alternative to Rage. He can deal high damage on offense or defense, and act as a tank for the player's push before activating its Rage, but he costs 2 more Elixir, and the player has less control over when and where the spell's effect takes place.
*Rage's effect does not stack with another Rage spell, the Lumberjack's dropped Rage spell, the built-in [[Buff#Rage|Rage buff]] from raged troops, or the Rage effect of the [[Barbarians/Evolution|Evolved Barbarians]]. However, the effect of Rage does stack with the environmental Rage boost of [[Global Spell|Rage Battles]].
*Under the influence of Rage, an [[X-Bow]] can shoot 4 projectiles every second, dealing massive damage to the opposing Crown Tower. This can be risky however, so only cast the Rage if you notice that the opponent does not react to the X-Bow in time.
*Troops or buildings with additional effects in their attacks can benefit greatly from Rage, allowing their effects to activate more frequently.
**Stunning cards, like the [[Electro Wizard]] will be able to stun the enemy troops more frequently, buying more time for the player to defeat. However, even with Rage, they cannot reset their attacks entirely, so they might still get hit.
**Similar to stunning cards, the [[Valkyrie/Evolution|Evolved Valkyrie]] and [[Mega Knight/Evolution|Evolved Mega Knight]] can make more uses of their pulling and pushing effects, and unlike the stunning cards, their attacks can reset the attacks of opposing troops. A [[Bowler]] or [[Executioner/Evolution|Evolved Executioner]] can work similarly.
**Troops that heal themselves when they attack, like the [[Battle Healer]] and [[Bats/Evolution|Evolved Bats]] will have increased longevity, allowing them to stay on the field for longer.
**With more frequent attacks, an [[Mortar/Evolution|Evolved Mortar]] will be able to spawn more Goblins, which will allow the player to overwhelm their opponent.
*Rage can be used to neutralize slowing effects, such as from the [[Ice Wizard]]. This might allow your troops to get closer to said Ice Wizard and be able to defeat him without taking too much damage.
*Do not use Rage on troops that are instantly defeated from their own attacks like the [[Ice Spirit]], [[Fire Spirit]], and [[Wall Breakers]], as this is a waste of 2 Elixir. An exception applies to ones that spawn other troops after death, such as the [[Battle Ram]] and [[Skeleton Barrel]].
*The Elixir Collector is affected by Rage, technically allowing it to produce Elixir faster. However, it is not enough to produce even a single Elixir due to its duration. In order to produce additional Elixir, 3 Rage spells are needed. This results in a massive 5 Elixir deficit, and thus is an ineffective strategy.
** Other spawner buildings can similarly result in additional waves of troops being spawned from them. The Barbarian Hut will not spawn additional waves, but it will result in the last wave spawning additional Barbarians. However, like the Elixir Collector, using the Rage spell just to spawn additional waves is an ineffective strategy.
*Since Rage's duration is identical at all Levels and its damage is quite low, upgrading it is generally wasteful if the player wishes to only boost friendly troops. At equal Levels, a Rage spell deal enough damage to OHKO the Spear Goblins, and a Level 14 Rage spell can OHKO Level 15 Spear Goblins. Therefore, it is recommended that the player invest their {{Rarity|Epic}} resources, (i.e., [[Magic Items|Wild Cards]] or [[Trade Tokens]]) into other {{Rarity|Epic}} cards first. However, a Level 14 Rage cannot OHKO [[Mirror|Mirrored]] Level 16 Spear Goblins, so the player should consider levelling it to 15.

