==History==
2016
*The Rage [[Cards|card]] was added with Clash Royale's game launch on 4/1/2016 {{Balance|Add}}.
*On 29/2/2016, the [[Version History#March 2016 Update (29/2/2016)|March 2016 Update]], added a falloff effect to Rage, causing [[:Category:Troop Cards|troops]] to lose the bonus if they are out of its effect for 2 seconds, whereas previously troops kept the effect permanently {{Balance|Add}}.
*On 23/3/2016, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (23/3/2016)|Balance Update]], increased the Rage's speed boost to 40% (from 35%) {{Balance|Buff}} and decreased its duration by 2 seconds {{Balance|Nerf}}. Its description was also changed to match the speed boost percentage number {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 3/5/2016, the [[Version History#May%202016%20Update%20(3/5/2016)|May 2016 Update]], changed the Rage's description. It used to say, ''“Increases troop movement and attack speed by 40%. Troop buildings and summoners deploy troops faster. Chaaaarge!''” {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 4/7/2016, the [[Version History#Tournaments Update (4/7/2016)|Tournaments Update]], allowed the [[Elixir Collector]] to be affected by Rage {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 19/9/2016, the [[Version History#September 2016 Update (19/9/2016)|September 2016 Update]], decreased the Rage's cost to 2 [[Elixir]] (from 3 Elixir) {{Balance|Buff}}, its speed boost to 30% (from 40%) {{Balance|Nerf}}, and its duration by 2 seconds {{Balance|Nerf}}. It also slightly changed its card description. It used to say, ''“Increases troop movement and attack speed. Troop buildings and summoners deploy troops faster. Chaaaarge!''” {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 1/11/2016, the [[Version History#November 2016 Update (1/11/2016)|November 2016 Update]], increased the Rage's speed boost to 35% (from 30%) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2018
*On 25/4/2018, the [[Version History#Clan%20Wars%20Update%20(25/4/2018)|Clan Wars Update]], allowed the Rage to be directly placed on the river {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 20/6/2018, the [[Version History#Summer%202018%20Update%20(20/6/2018)|Summer 2018 Update]], moved the [[Arenas|Arena]] to unlock the Rage from Spell Valley to Hog Mountain {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 5/9/2018, the [[Version History#September%202018%20Update%20(5/9/2018)|September 2018 Update]], changed it so that {{Rarity|Epic}} cards start at Level 6 and end at Level 13 (from 1 to 8) {{Balance|Neutral}}.
2019
*On 1/7/2019, the [[Version History#July%202019%20Update%20(1/7/2019)|July 2019 Update]], removed the Rage from all [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|Draft]] selections {{Balance|Remove}}.
2021
*On 7/6/2021, the [[Version History#Summer%202021%20Update%20(7/6/2021)|Summer 2021 Update]], moved the Arena to unlock the Rage from Hog Mountain to Serenity Peak {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 27/10/2021, the [[Version History#Champions%20Update%20(27/10/2021)|Champions Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 14 (from 13) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2022
*On 12/12/2022, the [[Version History#Clashmas Update (12/12/2022)|Clashmas Update]], set the Rage's duration to 6 seconds for every Level {{Balance|Neutral}} and made the [[:Category:Spell Cards|spell]] deal area damage {{Balance|Add}}. In addition, its area radius was decreased to 3 tiles (from 5 tiles) {{Balance|Nerf}}, and added a 0.5 second deploy timer to Rage {{Balance|Add}}.
2023
*On 4/1/2023, an [[Version History#Optional Update (4/1/2023)|Optional Update]], made the in-game visual effects of the Rage match the duration of the spell {{Balance|Neutral}}. It also fixed an issue where the Rage was considered a Troop card in its info menu {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 19/6/2023, the [[Version History#Card%20Evolution%20Update%20(19/6/2023)|Card Evolution Update]], increased the Level cap of all cards to 15 (from 14) {{Balance|Buff}}.
2024
*On 3/1/2024, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (3/1/2024)|Balance Update]], decreased the Rage's duration to 5.5 seconds (from 6 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
2025
*On 11/2/2025, a [[Version History#Maintenance Break (11/2/2025)|maintenance break]], made it so that [[Lumberjack/Evolution|Lumberjack Ghost]]'s lifetime is no longer affected by Rage {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 4/3/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (4/3/2025)|Balance Update]], decreased the Rage's duration after leaving the radius to 1 second (from 2 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 31/3/2025, the [[Version History#2025 Quarter 1 Update (31/3/2025)|2025 Quarter 1 Update]], allowed the [[Executioner]] and [[Ram Rider]] to be affected by Rage {{Balance|Neutral}}.
*On 9/4/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (9/4/2025)|Balance Update]], decreased the Rage's damage by 23% {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 4/8/2025, the [[Version History/2025#Pass Royale and more (4/8/2025)|August 2025 Update]] increased the Rage's damage by 21% {{Balance|Buff}}, but decreased its duration to 4.5 seconds (from 5.5 seconds) {{Balance|Nerf}}.
*On 6/10/2025, a [[Version History#Balance Changes (6/10/2025)=|Balance Update]] decreased the Rage's speed boost to 30% (from 35%).
2026

* On 1/6/2026, a Balance Update, decreased the Rage's Crown Tower damage to 25% of the full damage (from 30%)

