==Trivia== 
*The Rage is 1 of 7 [[:Category:Spell Cards|spells]] which first existed in Clash of Clans, the others being [[Earthquake]], [[Heal]], [[Lightning]], [[Freeze]], [[Poison]], and [[Clone]].
**Unlike its [https://clashofclans.fandom.com/wiki/Rage_Spell Clash of Clans counterpart], the Rage in Clash Royale deals damage and increases attacks speed instead of damage.
*The Rage, along with [[Wall Breakers]], [[Barbarian Barrel]], and [[Goblin Curse]], are the cheapest {{Rarity|Epic}} [[cards]], costing 2 [[Elixir]].
*In the Arabic, Persian, Indonesian, and Malaysian language settings of the game, the Rage's name translates to "Anger". In the Korean, Chinese, and Thai language settings of the game, the Rage's name translates to "Rage Magic", "Rage Spell", and "Mania" respectively.
*The Rage is 1 of 4 damaging spell [[cards]] that does not contain the phrase "''Reduced damage to Crown Towers.''" in its description despite dealing reduced damage to [[:Category:Crown Towers|Crown Towers]], with the others being Earthquake, Goblin Curse, and [[Tornado]].
*The Rage is 1 of 23 cards that has had its Elixir cost changed, the others being [[Bomber]], [[Fire Spirit]], [[Royal Recruits]], [[Cannon]], [[Mortar]], [[Musketeer]], [[Three Musketeers]], Heal, [[Goblin Hut]], [[Bomb Tower]], [[Barbarian Hut]], [[Furnace]], [[Elixir Collector]], [[Skeleton Army]], [[P.E.K.K.A.]], Wall Breakers, [[Electro Giant]], [[Bowler]], [[Goblin Barrel]], Barbarian Barrel, [[Fisherman]], and the [[Monk]].
*The Rage is 1 of 7 spells which have team-colored rings on their radius, the others are Earthquake, Freeze, Poison, Clone, Tornado, and [[Graveyard]].
**Along the perimeter of the spell, symbols will light up in sequence like a clock as the spell's duration continues.
*The Rage has been featured in multiple [[Tournament/Special Event Challenges|special game modes]] outside of the card. More specifically:
**The Rage is 1 of 4 spells that have been featured in the [[Global Spell]] game [[:Category:Modes|mode]], the others being Heal, Lightning, and Freeze.
**The Rage is 1 of 3 spells that have been featured in the [[Battleground#Boost Fields|Boost Fields]] sub-mode of the [[Battleground]] game mode, the others being Heal and Clone.
**The Rage is 1 of 5 spells that have been featured in the [[Treasure Hunt#Spell Cauldron|Spell Cauldron]] sub-mode of the [[Treasure Hunt]] game mode, the others being Heal, Lightning, Freeze, and Clone.
*The Rage, along with the Heal, Lightning, Freeze, and [[The Log]], are featured as a [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Spells spell] in [https://squad-busters.fandom.com/wiki/Squad_Busters_Wiki Squad Busters].
*Like its Clash of Clans counterpart, the Rage creates a "roaring" sound when casted, hence the name of the spell.
*When affected by Rage, a troop with a movement speed of Slow or Fast is enough to outpace a troop with a movement speed of Normal or Very Fast unaffected by the spell respectively. However, a troop with a movement speed of Very Slow or Normal is not enough to outpace a troop with a movement speed of Slow or Fast respectively.
*[[:Category:Troop Cards|Troops]] and certain buildings affected by the Rage will have their sounds played faster with a higher pitched effect. Slowdown effects however, like that of the [[Ice Wizard]], will do the opposite.
*The [[Card Mastery]] task "Rage of Empires" is a reference to the [https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Age_of_Empires Age of Empires] games series.
*Units under the effect of Rage will have their level visible, even if said units are at full health.
*In the [https://youtu.be/zWW1dtcsDGk?si=Ytadsvv1hpz23v9y Card Mastery intro video], the Rage's All the Rage Card Mastery task was shown to require raged troops to deal 427,000 damage. However, it was lowered to 425,000 in-game.
*On 12/12/2022, the Rage was supposed to be added higher damage and a pushback of 0.3 tiles, but it [https://royaleapi.com/blog/season-42-balance-wip was pulled back last minute].
*Before the Rage's card release, the Rage's duration was increased by 1 second.


